{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CesWikiAD7poorKkk4hZV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my exploration, let me document my findings:\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- Error handling: sealed ApiException hierarchy with ResourceNotFoundException (404), ConflictException (409)\n- GlobalExceptionHandler centrally converts exceptions to ApiError responses\n- Controllers throw exceptions; handlers build response bodies (lines 16-28 in GlobalExceptionHandler.kt)\n- Error codes are part of public API contract (ErrorCode enum in ApiError.kt:31-37)\n- Tests use MockMvc with status() and jsonPath() assertions (ShipmentControllerTest.kt patterns)\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` - add POST `/shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint\n2. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - add tests for all four cases (CREATED→CONFIRMED, already CONFIRMED, CANCELLED conflict, 404)\n3. `ApiError.kt` - add new error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` for cancelled/wrong state cases\n\n**Risks:**\n- If the idempotent retry behavior isn't correct, operations will fail on retries\n- Wrong error code might break client contracts\n- State transition logic must handle all three status values correctly\n\n**Open questions:**\n- None; requirement clearly specifies all four cases and their HTTP responses\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to ErrorCode enum. This handles the case where a shipment cannot be confirmed due to its current state (e.g., already CANCELLED).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new endpoint `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` that:\n   - Retrieves the shipment by ID (throws ResourceNotFoundException if not found)\n   - Checks if status is CANCELLED (throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE)\n   - If status is CREATED, updates it to CONFIRMED and saves\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, does nothing (idempotent)\n   - Returns the shipment in both success cases\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four test cases:\n   - Confirm CREATED shipment → 200 OK, status becomes CONFIRMED\n   - Confirm already CONFIRMED shipment → 200 OK, unchanged (idempotent)\n   - Confirm CANCELLED shipment → 409 Conflict with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code\n   - Confirm non-existent shipment → 404 Not Found with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\nI considered adding a helper method in the repository like `updateStatus()`, but the simple approach of calling `repository.save()` with a modified shipment is idiomatic for this immutable data class design and keeps the repository interface minimal.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n- GET: Controller calls `repository.findById()` → throws ResourceNotFoundException if null\n- CREATED state: Create new Shipment with status=CONFIRMED, call `repository.save()`\n- CONFIRMED state: Skip modification, return existing shipment\n- CANCELLED state: Throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE before database access\n- Response: All success cases return 200 OK with shipment JSON body\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1132,"cache_read_input_tokens":15266,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1132},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72d0db4f-0a50-44df-9ae9-d00fd6edf755","uuid":"85fec869-2a8b-4ec4-986c-b05e868fb936","timestamp":"2026-09-09T08:00:38.448Z","request_id":"req_011CesWijfeoUP4mTJ9agx2i"}
